# Smíðja — the smithy's own settings. THE SHAPE LIVES HERE; THE VALUES DO NOT.
#
# This repo is public and agnostic: it ships the template and a generic default
# (server/chat.ts · DEFAULT_CHAT_MODEL). What one operator wants their smithy to do is
# their own shape, so the real file lives in their home:
#
#   cp config/smidja.env.example  $YMIR_HOME/config/smidja.env
#
# Nothing secret belongs in it — a secret is referenced through the vault, never written.
# An environment variable of the same name wins over the file (a unit or a wrapper that
# knows better), and the file wins over the repo's default.

# The model Kaia's orchestrator chat starts on, and the one the picker shows selected.
# It must be a model this machine's pi actually serves; ask before you guess:
#
#   bin/model/catalog.sh --has opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash
#
SMIDJA_CHAT_MODEL=opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash
